    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is coherent and lands the logic in the right place \u2014 `generateCustomerCode` is the correct unit, and leaving the membership-number formatter to inherit the new prefix (only touching its Javadoc example) is exactly right, since it derives from `customerCode` and needs no logic change.\n\nOne structural finding:\n\n- **Duplicated abbreviation logic.** The `substring(0, Math.min(3, x.length())).toUpperCase()` \"first three letters, upper-cased\" expression now appears twice \u2014 once for `city3` and once for `last3`:\n  ```java\n  String city3 = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();\n  ...\n  String last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();\n  ```\n  Before this change it appeared once; the spec's addition of the CITY3 component has copied it. Extract a small private helper to keep it single-sourced, e.g.:\n  ```java\n  private static String prefix3(String value) {\n      return value.substring(0, Math.min(3, value.length())).toUpperCase();\n  }\n  ```\n  Then the method body reads `String city3 = prefix3(city);` / `String last3 = prefix3(lastName);`. This keeps the two segment-derivation rules identical by construction and makes the code path additive rather than copy-pasted.\n\nAside from that, the format string and per-city sequence composition read naturally for this codebase.",
